,"lemma":"āṅku","gloss":"there"},{"text":"அவர்","lemma":"avar","gloss":"they"}],"gloss":"those people"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தமதெனத்","parts":[{"text":"தமது","lemma":"tamatu","gloss":"theirs"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"saying"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"saying 'it is ours'"},{"surface":"தொடுக்குவர்","parts":[{"text":"தொடுக்குவர்","lemma":"toṭukkuvar","gloss":"if they claim"}],"gloss":"if they claim"},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if so"}],"gloss":"if so"},{"surface":"எமதெனப்","parts":[{"text":"எமது","lemma":"ematu","gloss":"ours"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"saying"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"saying 'it is ours'"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பற்றல்","parts":[{"text":"பற்றல்","lemma":"paṟṟal","gloss":"claiming"}],"gloss":"claiming"},{"surface":"தேற்றாப்","parts":[{"text":"தேற்றா","lemma":"tēṟṟā","gloss":"not knowing how to hold back"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"not knowing how to hold back"},{"surface":"பயங்கெழு","parts":[{"text":"பயம்","lemma":"payam","gloss":"wealth"},{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"keḻu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"wealth-yielding"},{"surface":"தாயமொடு","parts":[{"text":"தாயம்","lemma":"tāyam","gloss":"domain"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with your domain"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"aṉṉa","gloss":"such"}],"gloss":"such"},{"surface":"வாக","parts":[{"text":"வாக","lemma":"வாக","gloss":"let it be"}],"gloss":"let it be","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"ஊழி","parts":[{"text":"ஊழி","lemma":"ūḻi","gloss":"lifetime"}],"gloss":"lifetime"},{"surface":"நின்னைக்","parts":[{"text":"நின்னை","lemma":"niṉṉai","gloss":"you"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காண்டல்","parts":[{"text":"காண்டல்","lemma":"kāṇṭal","gloss":"seeing"}],"gloss":"seeing"},{"surface":"வேண்டிய","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டிய","lemma":"vēṇṭiya","gloss":"desired"}],"gloss":"desired"},{"surface":"அளவை","parts":[{"text":"அளவை","lemma":"aḷavai","gloss":"extent"}],"gloss":"extent"},{"surface":"வேண்டார்","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டார்","lemma":"vēṇṭār","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உறுமுரண்","parts":[{"text":"உறு","lemma":"uṟu","gloss":"great"},{"text":"முரண்","lemma":"muraṇ","gloss":"enmity"}],"gloss":"great enmity"},{"surface":"கடந்த","parts":[{"text":"கடந்த","lemma":"கடந்த","gloss":"conquered"}],"gloss":"conquered","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆற்றல்","parts":[{"text":"ஆற்றல்","lemma":"āṟṟal","gloss":"power"}],"gloss":"power"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொதுமீக்","parts":[{"text":"பொது","lemma":"potu","gloss":"common"},{"text":"மீ","lemma":"mī","gloss":"above"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"above all common rulers"},{"surface":"கூற்றத்து","parts":[{"text":"கூற்றத்து","lemma":"கூற்றத்து","gloss":"of the proclamation"}],"gloss":"of the proclamation","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாடுகிழ","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"nāṭu","gloss":"country"},{"text":"கிழ","lemma":"kiḻa","gloss":"owner"}],"gloss":"lord of the land"},{"surface":"வோயே","parts":[{"text":"வோயே","lemma":"ōyē","gloss":"O lord (vocative)"}],"gloss":"O lord!"}]}],"literal":"Where tigers with curved stripes roam, on the high-peaked tall mountain / climbing the narrow path of difficult distress, suffering / with a faltering gait and graceful soft steps / my bangle-wearing female dancer following behind me / with tightly twisted strings like drawn gold / playing melodies of songs, moving from place to place to sound / the small lute of sweet Paṭumalai mode / holding it on one side with a weary heart / thinking of your good fame of abundant excellence / I came, my lord, and always saying / if you see suppliants present in your court, along with calves / you drive away mortar-footed elephants / O Āy, the great chieftain of the mountainous country! / Even male elephants are not yours, even horses are not yours / even chariots with horses and shining weapons are not yours / bards, singers, and suppliants, those people / if they claim them as theirs, saying 'it is ours' / with your wealth-yielding domain that knows not how to hold back / let it be so during your lifetime! You / to see you is all they desired, but your enemies / with power that conquered great enmity / O lord of the land, who stands above all common rulers!","translation":"My bangle-wearing dancer followed behind me, taking slow, graceful steps with a faltering gait, exhausted from climbing the narrow, difficult paths of the high-peaked mountain where striped tigers roam. Holding on one side with a weary heart our small lute of sweet Paṭumalai mode, whose tightly twisted strings shine like drawn gold, we played melodies that echoed as we moved. Thinking of your great fame, my lord, I came here. O Āy, great chieftain of the mountainous land! When you see suppliants in your court, you give away mortar-footed elephants along with their calves, driving them out to them. Indeed, those male elephants are not yours, those horses are not yours, and those chariots with shining weapons are not yours either! If bards, singers, and suppliants claim them as theirs, you do not know how to hold them back, saying 'they are ours'—such is your wealth-yielding domain! May your lifetime be blessed! Your enemies, whose great strength you conquered with your power, desire only to see you and nothing else, O lord of the land who stands supreme above all common rulers!","modern":"வளைந்த வரிகளையுடைய புலிகள் நடமாடும், சிகரங்கள் உயர்ந்த நீண்ட மலையின் துன்பம் நிறைந்த குறுகிய பாதையில் ஏறியதால் வருத்தமடைந்து, தளர்ந்த நடையுடனும் மென்மையான அழகிய அடிகளுடனும் வளைந்த வளையல்களை அணிந்த என் விறலி எனக்குப் பின்னால் வர, பொன்னைக் காய்ச்சி வடித்தது போன்ற முறுக்கேறிய நரம்புகளைக் கொண்ட, படுமலைப் பாலையாகிய இனிய இசையைத் தரும் சிறிய யாழினை ஒரு பக்கமாக அணைத்துக் கொண்டு, உன்னுடைய புகழை நினைத்து என் தலைவனே நான் இங்கு வந்தேன். மலைகள் நிறைந்த நாட்டின் தலைவனான மாவேள் ஆய் அண்டிரனே! உனது அவையில் இருக்கும் இரவலர்களைக் கண்டால், கன்றுகளுடன் கூடிய பெரிய கால்களைக் கொண்ட யானைகளை அவர்களுக்குப் பரிசாகக் கொடுத்து அனுப்புவாய். உன்னுடைய களிறுகளும், குதிரைகளும், ஒளிரும் படைகளைக் கொண்ட தேர்களும் உனக்குரியவை அல்ல! பாணர்களும், பாடுபவர்களும், இரவலர்களும் அவற்றை 'எங்களுடையவை' என்று உரிமை கொண்டாடினால், 'இவை எமக்கே உரியவை' என்று தடுத்து நிறுத்தத் தெரியாத வளம் பொருந்திய நாட்டை உடையவன் நீ. உனது வாழ்நாள் முழுவதும் இவ்வாறே கொடைத்திறம் நிலைத்திருக்கட்டும்! உன்னுடைய பேராற்றலால் வெல்லப்பட்ட பகைவர்கள் உன்னைக் காண்பதையே விரும்புவார்கள், வேறு எதையும் விரும்ப மாட்டார்கள்; பொதுவான அரசர்களுக்கு மேலாக விளங்கும் நாட்டின் தலைவனே!","explanation":"The poet Uṟaiyūr Ēṇiccēri Muṭamōciyār addresses the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ in this Pāṭāṇ tiṇai poem. He describes the arduous journey he and his female dancer (viraḷi) undertook through steep, tiger-infested mountain paths to reach Āy's court, carrying their small lute (ciṟiyāḻ). Upon arrival, the poet praises Āy's extraordinary generosity, noting that he gives away elephants, horses, and chariots so freely that they seem to belong to the suppliants rather than to Āy himself. Even his defeated enemies desire only to see him, acknowledging his supreme status above all other rulers. Key words include 'விறலி' (female dancer), 'சீறியாழ்' (small lute), and 'மாவேள் ஆஅய்' (great chieftain Āy).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[0.8,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.4],[2.4,3.58],[3.76,4.0],[4.0,4.53],[4.53,5.3],[5.3,5.6],[5.6,6.1],[6.1,6.5],[6.5,6.9],[7.03,7.17],[7.17,7.83],[7.97,8.1],[8.1,8.79],[8.79,9.2],[9.2,10.1],[10.1,10.3],[10.3,11.41],[11.41,12.3],[12.3,12.9],[12.9,13.3],[13.3,13.87],[13.87,14.3],[14.3,14.7],[14.7,15.2],[15.2,16.02],[16.29,16.7],[16.7,17.56],[17.56,17.9],[18.56,19.16],[19.16,19.96],[19.96,20.26],[20.26,20.76],[20.76,21.86],[21.86,22.16],[22.16,22.46],[22.62,22.96],[22.96,23.45],[23.45,24.43],[24